## ANOVA in R

### Fitting the model

::: {.codewindow .r .codewindow-dark}
anova.R


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
# aov(DV ~ IV, data): the group column must be a factor
fit <- aov(iq ~ group, data = ssld)

summary(fit)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
             Df Sum Sq Mean Sq F value  Pr(>F)   
group         2   2867    1433    6.37 0.00195 **
Residuals   297  66825     225                   
---
Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1
```


:::
:::

:::

-   `Df`: degrees of freedom ($k - 1$ between, $N - k$ within)

-   `Sum Sq`, `Mean Sq`: the SS and MS ($MS = SS/df$)

-   `F value`: $MS_B / MS_E$ and `Pr(>F)`: its p-value

