## Post-hoc Tests

### A significant F tells us *some* means differ, not *which*

::: {.codewindow .r .codewindow-dark}
tukey.R


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
# Tukey's HSD compares every pair and adjusts for multiple comparisons
TukeyHSD(fit)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
  Tukey multiple comparisons of means
    95% family-wise confidence level

Fit: aov(formula = iq ~ group, data = ssld)

$group
                diff        lwr       upr     p adj
Placebo-SSLD      -6 -10.996823 -1.003177 0.0138048
Control-SSLD      -7 -11.996823 -2.003177 0.0031068
Control-Placebo   -1  -5.996823  3.996823 0.8847861
```


:::
:::

:::

-   `diff` is the difference between the two group means.

-   `p adj` is adjusted for the number of comparisons, so the familywise error rate stays at 5%.

